## Phase 3: Technical Prep

### What to Expect Based on Role

| Role | Focus Areas |
|------|-------------|
| **MLE** | Production systems, model serving, data pipelines, MLOps |
| **Data Scientist** | E2E ML lifecycle, business translation, statistics |
| **Research Scientist** | Papers, novel methods, deep theory |
| **ML Engineer** | Python, PyTorch, system design, deployment |

### Key Topics to Review

#### ML Theory (Your Strengths)
- Loss functions (BCE, Focal Loss, weighted approaches)
- Class imbalance handling
- Model evaluation (precision, recall, F1, calibration)
- Regularization, overfitting
- Transformers, attention mechanisms

#### System Design
- Model serving architecture
- Data pipeline design
- Inference optimization
- Scaling considerations

#### Coding (LeetCode)
- Python proficiency
- Data structures, algorithms
- SQL basics
- PyTorch tensor operations

---

## Phase 4: Your 3-Day Prep Plan

### Day 1: Fundamentals + Company Research
| Time | Activity |
|------|----------|
| 30 min | Review loss functions (your Focal Loss notes) |
| 30 min | Company research (prioritize what they do) |
| 45 min | 2 LeetCode problems (medium) |
| 30 min | Practice 2 STAR stories out loud |

### Day 2: Projects + System Design
| Time | Activity |
|------|----------|
| 45 min | Prepare project walkthrough (pick 1, make it 2 min) |
| 30 min | System design: model serving basics |
| 30 min | Review your GitHub, know your code |
| 15 min | Mock one behavioral question |

### Day 3: Mock + Confidence
| Time | Activity |
|------|----------|
| 30 min | Review metrics (precision, recall, calibration) |
| 45 min | Full mock interview (or self-recorded) |
| 30 min | Prepare 3 questions for interviewer |
| 15 min | Rest, breathe, trust your prep |

---

## Phase 5: Quick Wins (Before Interview)

### High-Impact Actions

| Action | Time | Why |
|--------|------|-----|
| Update GitHub README | 1 hr | Shows communication, code ownership |
| Write 1-pager on SportsNGEN | 1 hr | Demonstrates research + engineering |
| Practice STAR out loud | 30 min | Builds confidence, catches gaps |
| Company research doc | 30 min | Shows genuine interest |

### Questions to Ask Interviewer

1. "What's the biggest ML challenge your team faces right now?"
2. "How does your team approach model deployment and monitoring?"
3. "What's the balance between research and production work?"

---

## Common Pitfalls & How to Avoid

| Pitfall | Solution |
|---------|----------|
| Generic answers | Use your specific metrics ("90.5% confidence") |
| No questions | Prepare 3 ahead of time |
| Skipping fundamentals | Review your Focal Loss experiments |
| Not connecting to company | Spend 30 min researching |
| Jargon without explanation | Assume they need simple language |

